23970>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
23970>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This only gets called when the developer is killing this object. During application
23970>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // shut-down, only destroy_object is called. This augmentation destroys the watched broadcaster
23970>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (which is sitting on the desktop). During program shut down we don't care if this is called
23970>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // because it is getting destroyed anyway. We are making the assumption that a developer controlled
23970>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // destroy will always be called with the watcher still existing.
23970>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Destroy
23972>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatched
23972>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Changed_State to False //   is this really needed anymore???
23973>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The watched server, must still exist.
23973>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatched
23974>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
23976>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
23977>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the broadcaster
23978>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
23978>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
23978>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The bound watched server, must still exist.
23978>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatched
23979>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
23981>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
23982>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the broadcaster
23983>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
23983>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
23983>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Destroy
23985>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
23986>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
23986>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Required DD/DEO interface
23986>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // sent by DD before a find and save. We only care about DD finds which
23986>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // means DoAll is 1
23986>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Entry_Update Integer iFile Integer iDoAll
23988>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure scans the fields of this object's items to determine
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   what other database agents (data_sets) other than this object's Server
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   should be 'watched' (for data changes).
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   iTableFlag is a boolean determining whether this object relies on a
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   prototype row (TRUE) or an item list (FALSE).
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   [JVH] VDF 17.0 - Ignored in this class.
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This object must understand pbDataBindable, and have a private
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   boolean property named Private_pbServersScanned to note the event.
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Notes
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure is invoked once per object, the first time the object
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   is activated.  If the data_file, data_field, and/or main_file of this
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   object are changed (don't change them while this object is active!),
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set Private_pbServersScanned to FALSE to force this object to scan
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   again (when it is next activated).
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 17.0: The logic has been retooled to add more watched servers to the DDOs. This is done so
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // DD operations will send Refresh to these additional watched-servers. There are two changes:
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 1. Containers are now made watched servers for the Server and all parent servers
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 2. Non-file.field DEOs (e.g., expressions) are made watched servers for the server (which it
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    already did and for all parent servers. Without this, parent entry_item expressions were not
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    getting updated
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Here is how watched-servers works.
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Each DEO attaches and detaches from its Server by sending Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to the server DD. Once attached, the DD knows about this DEO and sends messages to it as needed (Refresh,
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Entry_Update, etc.). In addition, a DEO may need to attach a parent DDO so that changes in that parent DD
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // results in those messages being sent. This is needed if the binding table in entry_item refers to a parent
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // table. So we need to send Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface to that parent server as well. If a DEO
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // has multiple, there could be multiple parent servers. As of 17.0, we are also attaching to parent servers if
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // we are unsure about how the DEO is being used. If an expression is used, it might need to be updated when
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // a parent (or any ancestor) changes. Each DEO keeps track of servers that it attaches to and this is referred
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to as the watched_server list. This list is maintained so the DEO knows which DDOs to attach and detach to.
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // [JVH] VDF 17.1 cWebAppDEOServer_mixin Notes:
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // - Modified to support only 1 item per control. Get Item_Count interface not supported.
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // - Modified to not support the Prototype_Object interface (old windows Table class).
23989>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_Servers_To_Watch Integer iTableFlag
23991>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFileNum iServerFile
23991>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer hoDataSet
23991>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataBindable
23991>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
23991>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataBindable to bDataBindable
23992>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Private_pbServersScanned to True
23993>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
23994>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
23994>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer = 0) Begin
23996>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
23997>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
23997>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
23997>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
23997>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Delete_Watched_Servers  // empty Watched_Servers broadcaster first
23998>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoServer to iServerFile  // data-set's main-file
23999>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
23999>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bDataBindable)) Begin
24001>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // containers should get added to all parent DDOs
24001>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers hoServer
24002>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
24003>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
24003>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
24003>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
24003>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_File to iFileNum
24004>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // we need watched server if file exists, it is not the main file
24004>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // and is not an updating file (as opposed to updating data-set).
24004>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iFileNum > 0 and iFileNum <> iServerFile) Begin
24006>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Which_Data_Set of hoServer iFileNum to hoDataSet
24007>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (hoDataSet <> 0 and hoDataSet <> hoServer) Begin
24009>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Add_Watched_Server hoDataSet
24010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Add_ChangedStateWatched_Server hoDataSet
24011>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
24011>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
24011>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
24011>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
24011>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iFileNum = 0) Begin
24014>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if no file (e.g., expression) we don't know when it changes so we tell all servers
24014>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // that this is a watcher
24014>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers hoServer
24015>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
24015>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
24015>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
24016>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
24016>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function returns the object id of the database agent of this object,
24016>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // or 0.
24016>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Locate_Server Returns Integer
24018>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
24018>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
24019>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoServer
24020>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
24021>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
24021>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Refresh Integer eMode
24023>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
24024>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
24024>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure discontinues the connection between this object and its
24024>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   database agent(s) (Server and Watched_Servers).
24024>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Remove_DEO_From_Server
24026>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoServer hoWatchedServers
24026>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
24026>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
24027>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
24027>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer <> 0) Begin
24029>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to hoServer Self
24030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
24030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
24030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
24030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Only send if watched-server exists
24030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
24031>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
24031>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
24033>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to hoWatchedServers Self True // TRUE for watchers
24034>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
24034>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
24034>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
24034>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // when removed the deo is no longer up to date.
24034>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Refresh_Dirty_State to True
24035>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
24036>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
24036>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure removes the specified object id (hoServer) from this object's
24036>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set of database agents who are merely 'watched', and destroys the
24036>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   connection between the database agent and this object.
24036>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Remove_Watched_Server Integer hoServer
24038>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
24038>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatchedServers
24038>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
24038>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
24039>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Only if w server exists
24039>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
24041>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to False
24042>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get find_element of hoWatchedServers hoServer to iIndex
24043>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iIndex >= 0) Begin
24045>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send remove_element to hoWatchedServers hoServer
24046>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
24046>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
24046>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to True
24047>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iIndex >= 0 and Active_State(Self)) Begin
24049>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Remove_User_Interface to hoServer Self True // TRUE for watchers
24050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
24050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
24050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
24050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
