24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Sent by DDO when there is a clear/find/save/delete.
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This should Set all necessary web properties of the control
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // For example pbEnabled.
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // eMode - Determines the type of DDO operation which generated this refresh message. 
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //         It may be one of the following:
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Clear:             Used only for DEOs attached to the DDO that was the
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //                                 "origin" of a Clear operation, (i.e., the DDO received
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //                                 the original Clear message). All other DDOs Send their 
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //                                 DEOs the refresh message passing mode_find_or_clear_set.  
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Find_or_Clear_Set: Used for DEOs attached to DDOs which have Found and/or cleared records.  
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Clear_All:         Used for DEOs attached to any DDO that participated in a clear_all operation.  
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Delete:            Used for DEOs attached to any DDO that performed a successful deletion. 
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //                                 DDOs that were merely updated as the result of a deletion Use Mode_Find_or_Clear_Set.  
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Save:              Used for DEOs attached to any DDO involved in a successful Save operation. 
24204>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Refresh Integer eMode
24206>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
