26866>>>>>>>>>
26866>>>>>>>>>
26866>>>>>>>>>    // RegisterColumn:
26866>>>>>>>>>    
26866>>>>>>>>>    // Registers a column object in the columns collection.
26866>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RegisterColumn Handle hoColumn
26868>>>>>>>>>        Integer iSize
26868>>>>>>>>>        Handle[] hoColumnObjects
26869>>>>>>>>>        Get phoColumnObjects to hoColumnObjects
26870>>>>>>>>>        Move (SizeOfArray(hoColumnObjects)) to iSize
26871>>>>>>>>>        Move hoColumn to hoColumnObjects[iSize]
26872>>>>>>>>>        Set piColumnId of hoColumn to iSize
26873>>>>>>>>>        Set phoColumnObjects to hoColumnObjects
26874>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26875>>>>>>>>>    
26875>>>>>>>>>    
26875>>>>>>>>>    // Sent by DDO when there is a clear/find/save/delete.
26875>>>>>>>>>    //
26875>>>>>>>>>    // eMode - Determines the type of DDO operation which generated this refresh message. 
26875>>>>>>>>>    //         It may be one of the following:
26875>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Clear:             Used only for DEOs attached to the DDO that was the
26875>>>>>>>>>    //                                 "origin" of a Clear operation, (i.e., the DDO received
26875>>>>>>>>>    //                                 the original Clear message). All other DDOs Send their 
26875>>>>>>>>>    //                                 DEOs the refresh message passing mode_find_or_clear_set.  
26875>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Find_or_Clear_Set: Used for DEOs attached to DDOs which have Found and/or cleared records.  
26875>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Clear_All:         Used for DEOs attached to any DDO that participated in a clear_all operation.  
26875>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Delete:            Used for DEOs attached to any DDO that performed a successful deletion. 
26875>>>>>>>>>    //                                 DDOs that were merely updated as the result of a deletion Use Mode_Find_or_Clear_Set.  
26875>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Save:              Used for DEOs attached to any DDO involved in a successful Save operation. 
26875>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Refresh Integer eMode
26877>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMainFile
26877>>>>>>>>>        Integer eDDStatus
26877>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDDO
26877>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bActive bAppSynching bMainFound
26877>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bRowDisplay bInClearGrid bDataAware 
26877>>>>>>>>>        Integer eDBGridType
26877>>>>>>>>>        String sCurrentRowID
26877>>>>>>>>>        RowID riCurrentRowID riID
26877>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCurrentRowIndex
26877>>>>>>>>>        
26877>>>>>>>>>        Get Active_State to bActive
26878>>>>>>>>>        Get AppSynching to bAppSynching
26879>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26880>>>>>>>>>        Get peDbGridType to eDBGridType
26881>>>>>>>>>
26881>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware and bActive and not(bAppSynching)) Begin
26883>>>>>>>>>            Get ReadingServer to hoDDO                  // hoDDO cannot be 0 otherwise we would never receive Refresh!
26884>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoDDO to iMainFile
26885>>>>>>>>>        
26885>>>>>>>>>            Get DDRefreshTableStatus iMainFile to eDDStatus
26886>>>>>>>>>            Move (eDDStatus <> ddrtsNone) to bMainFound     // True = a main dd find or constrained child dd find has occurred
26887>>>>>>>>>            Get pbNotifyingExternalDD to bRowDisplay                 // True = we are simply responding to a change of the current row ID on the client
26888>>>>>>>>>            
26888>>>>>>>>>            // Get the current row's row id
26888>>>>>>>>>            WebGet psCurrentRowId to sCurrentRowID
26889>>>>>>>>>            Move (DeserializeRowID(sCurrentRowID)) to riCurrentRowID
26890>>>>>>>>>            WebGet piCurrentRowIndex to iCurrentRowIndex
26891>>>>>>>>>        
26891>>>>>>>>>            // Handle the case where there is no selected row and we've done a save or delete on the main file.
26891>>>>>>>>>            // We don't know what to do in this case so we will refresh the grid. This could happen if the save
26891>>>>>>>>>            // is occuring from an external source (e.g., create a new record directly in the DD)
26891>>>>>>>>>            If (iCurrentRowIndex=-1 and (eMode = MODE_SAVE or eMode = MODE_DELETE) and bMainFound and (not(bRowDisplay))) Begin
26893>>>>>>>>>                Move MODE_FIND_OR_CLEAR_SET to eMode
26894>>>>>>>>>            End
26894>>>>>>>>>>
26894>>>>>>>>>
26894>>>>>>>>>            // If this is a clear on the grid's main file and it is not grid insert/append row, all we can do is clear and refresh the grid
26894>>>>>>>>>            Get pbInClearGrid to bInClearGrid
26895>>>>>>>>>            If (bInClearGrid) Begin
26897>>>>>>>>>                Move MODE_FIND_OR_CLEAR_SET to eMode
26898>>>>>>>>>            End
26898>>>>>>>>>>
26898>>>>>>>>>
26898>>>>>>>>>            If (eMode = MODE_CLEAR and bMainFound and sCurrentRowID <> "") Begin
26900>>>>>>>>>                //  HW: Added check for empty current row id which prevents recursive clearing with two grids on a single DD.
26900>>>>>>>>>                // special case with clear. If this comes from some other DEO (which is unusual)
26900>>>>>>>>>                // and the curent row has a record, then we need to insert a row for the
26900>>>>>>>>>                // cleared row.
26900>>>>>>>>>                If (not(bRowDisplay)) Begin
26902>>>>>>>>>                    Send AppendNewRow
26903>>>>>>>>>                End
26903>>>>>>>>>>
26903>>>>>>>>>                
26903>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26904>>>>>>>>>            End
26904>>>>>>>>>>
26904>>>>>>>>>            
26904>>>>>>>>>            Else If (eMode = MODE_DELETE or eMode = MODE_SAVE or bRowDisplay or not(bMainFound)) Begin
26907>>>>>>>>>                // Perform necessary actions for Save or Delete of a Grid Row
26907>>>>>>>>>                If (hoDDO = OPERATION_ORIGIN) Begin    // OPERATION_ORIGIN is the DDO that is the origin of the Save, Delete, find or clear
26909>>>>>>>>>                    // if a save notification and the save's DD is the same as the grid's
26909>>>>>>>>>                    // we are saving the main record and it may now be out of order
26909>>>>>>>>>                    If (eMode = MODE_SAVE) Begin
26911>>>>>>>>>                        WebSet pbUnOrdered to True
26912>>>>>>>>>                    End
26912>>>>>>>>>>
26912>>>>>>>>>                End
26912>>>>>>>>>>
26912>>>>>>>>>
26912>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26913>>>>>>>>>            End
26913>>>>>>>>>>
26913>>>>>>>>>            
26913>>>>>>>>>            Else If (eMode = MODE_CLEAR_ALL) Begin
26916>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26917>>>>>>>>>                If (eDBGridType<>gtManual) Begin
26919>>>>>>>>>                    Send ClearFilter
26920>>>>>>>>>                    Send EmptyGridRefresh
26921>>>>>>>>>                End
26921>>>>>>>>>>
26921>>>>>>>>>            End
26921>>>>>>>>>>
26921>>>>>>>>>            Else If (eMode = MODE_FIND_OR_CLEAR_SET) Begin
26924>>>>>>>>>                // If we got here then refresh the entire grid
26924>>>>>>>>>                Move (GetRowID(iMainFile)) to riID
26925>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26926>>>>>>>>>                If (eDBGridType<>gtManual) Begin
26928>>>>>>>>>                    Send GridRefresh
26929>>>>>>>>>                End
26929>>>>>>>>>>
26929>>>>>>>>>                Send ReadByRowId of hoDDO iMainFile riID
26930>>>>>>>>>            End
26930>>>>>>>>>>
26930>>>>>>>>>        End
26930>>>>>>>>>>
26930>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26931>>>>>>>>>    
26931>>>>>>>>>    /*    Refresh event during intialization of FlexTron controls. Latches onto the current record buffer     which may not have been recently found.    */
26931>>>>>>>>>    Procedure InitialRefresh
26933>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bActive bAppSynching bDataAware
26933>>>>>>>>>        Integer eDBGridType iMainFile
26933>>>>>>>>>        Handle  hoDDO
26933>>>>>>>>>        RowID riID
26933>>>>>>>>>        
26933>>>>>>>>>        Get Active_State to bActive
26934>>>>>>>>>        Get AppSynching to bAppSynching
26935>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26936>>>>>>>>>        Get peDbGridType to eDBGridType
26937>>>>>>>>>
26937>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware and bActive and not(bAppSynching)) Begin
26939>>>>>>>>>            Get ReadingServer to hoDDO                  // hoDDO cannot be 0 otherwise we would never receive Refresh!
26940>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoDDO to iMainFile
26941>>>>>>>>>            
26941>>>>>>>>>            // If we got here then refresh the entire grid
26941>>>>>>>>>            Move (GetRowID(iMainFile)) to riID
26942>>>>>>>>>            Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26943>>>>>>>>>            If (eDBGridType<>gtManual) Begin
26945>>>>>>>>>                Send GridRefresh
26946>>>>>>>>>            End
26946>>>>>>>>>>
26946>>>>>>>>>            Send ReadByRowId of hoDDO iMainFile riID
26947>>>>>>>>>        End
26947>>>>>>>>>>
26947>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26948>>>>>>>>>    
26948>>>>>>>>>    
26948>>>>>>>>>    // Does nothing in cWebList. See ClearSelectedRow in cWebGrid class.
26948>>>>>>>>>    // returns True.
26948>>>>>>>>>    Function ClearSelectedRow Returns Boolean
26950>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
26951>>>>>>>>>    End_Function  
26952>>>>>>>>>    
26952>>>>>>>>>    // Does nothing in cWebList. cWebList is read only. See SaveSelectedRow in cWebGrid class.
26952>>>>>>>>>    Function SaveSelectedRow Returns Integer
26954>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sroSucceed
26955>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
26956>>>>>>>>>    
26956>>>>>>>>>    // Delete Logic to delete the current row pointed to by psCurrentRowId.
26956>>>>>>>>>    // returns True if the delete was successful.
26956>>>>>>>>>    Function DeleteSelectedRow Returns Integer
26958>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
26958>>>>>>>>>        Handle hmVerify
26958>>>>>>>>>        RowID riCurrentRowID riTestRowID
26958>>>>>>>>>        String sCurrentRowID
26958>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering iMainFile
26958>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bReverseOrdering
26958>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataAware
26958>>>>>>>>>        Integer iReturn
26958>>>>>>>>>
26958>>>>>>>>>        WebGet psCurrentRowId to sCurrentRowID
26959>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26960>>>>>>>>>        
26960>>>>>>>>>        // db-aware handling
26960>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware) Begin
26962>>>>>>>>>            Get Server to hoDD
26963>>>>>>>>>            If (hoDD <> 0) Begin
26965>>>>>>>>>                Move (DeserializeRowID(sCurrentRowID)) to riCurrentRowID
26966>>>>>>>>>                Get CurrentRowId of hoDD to riTestRowID
26967>>>>>>>>>                
26967>>>>>>>>>                If (not(IsSameRowID(riCurrentRowID, riTestRowID))) Begin
26969>>>>>>>>>                    Error DFERR_PROGRAM "Assert: Server DDO's current record does not match psCurrentRowId"
26970>>>>>>>>>>
26970>>>>>>>>>                    Function_Return sroFail
26971>>>>>>>>>                End
26971>>>>>>>>>>
26971>>>>>>>>>                
26971>>>>>>>>>                // Verify that we are allowed to delete
26971>>>>>>>>>                If (Read_Only_State(hoDD) or not(pbAllowDeleteRow(Self)) or not(Can_Delete(hoDD))) Begin
26973>>>>>>>>>                    Function_Return sroFail         // the view should not allow this to happen
26974>>>>>>>>>                End
26974>>>>>>>>>>
26974>>>>>>>>>            End
26974>>>>>>>>>>
26974>>>>>>>>>        End
26974>>>>>>>>>>
26974>>>>>>>>>        
26974>>>>>>>>>        Get Verify_Delete_msg to hmVerify
26975>>>>>>>>>        If (hmVerify) Begin
26977>>>>>>>>>            WebSet pbDeleteCallbackActive to True
26978>>>>>>>>>            Send VerifyRequest (RefProc(RequestDeleteCallBack)) (RefFunc(Verify_Delete_Msg))
26979>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return sroPending
26980>>>>>>>>>        End
26980>>>>>>>>>>
26980>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
26981>>>>>>>>>            Send RequestDeleteExec
26982>>>>>>>>>            // we actually don't know if this will work or not, since this finds another row. For now, we say success
26982>>>>>>>>>        End
26982>>>>>>>>>>
26982>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sroSucceed
26983>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
26984>>>>>>>>>    
26984>>>>>>>>>    // This event is triggered by Request_Delete. It is intended to be implemented on grids having 
26984>>>>>>>>>    // pbDataAware set to false to process the delete. If the delete cannot be performed return 
26984>>>>>>>>>    // false to cancel the grid from removing the row from the display. Returning false when 
26984>>>>>>>>>    // pbDataAware is set to true will also cancel the delete from being sent to the DDO.
26984>>>>>>>>>    Function OnDeleteRow String sCurrentRowID Returns Boolean
26986>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
26987>>>>>>>>>    End_Function        
26988>>>>>>>>>
26988>>>>>>>>>    
26988>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RequestDeleteExec
26990>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
26990>>>>>>>>>        String sCurrentRowID
26990>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering iMainFile
26990>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bReverseOrdering
26990>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataAware bContinue
26990>>>>>>>>>
26990>>>>>>>>>        WebGet psCurrentRowId to sCurrentRowID
26991>>>>>>>>>        Get OnDeleteRow sCurrentRowID to bContinue
26992>>>>>>>>>        
26992>>>>>>>>>        // db-aware
26992>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26993>>>>>>>>>        
26993>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware) Begin
26995>>>>>>>>>            If (bContinue) Begin
26997>>>>>>>>>                // Perform the db-aware delete
26997>>>>>>>>>                Get Server to hoDD
26998>>>>>>>>>                Send Request_Delete to hoDD       // Perform the delete
26999>>>>>>>>>                            
26999>>>>>>>>>                If (Err) Begin
27001>>>>>>>>>                    Procedure_Return
27002>>>>>>>>>                End
27002>>>>>>>>>>
27002>>>>>>>>>                
27002>>>>>>>>>                Send RemoveRow sCurrentRowID      // Tell the client to remove the deleted row.
27003>>>>>>>>>                
27003>>>>>>>>>                // Select the next logical row
27003>>>>>>>>>                Get IndexOrder to iOrdering
27004>>>>>>>>>                WebGet pbReverseOrdering to bReverseOrdering
27005>>>>>>>>>                Get Main_File of hoDD to iMainFile
27006>>>>>>>>>        
27006>>>>>>>>>                If (bReverseOrdering) Begin
27008>>>>>>>>>                    Send Establish_Find_Direction of hoDD LT iMainFile iOrdering 
27009>>>>>>>>>                End
27009>>>>>>>>>>
27009>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
27010>>>>>>>>>                    Send Establish_Find_Direction of hoDD GT iMainFile iOrdering 
27011>>>>>>>>>                End
27011>>>>>>>>>>
27011>>>>>>>>>                
27011>>>>>>>>>                Send Locate_Next of hoDD    // Try to find the row below the deleted row.
27012>>>>>>>>>                
27012>>>>>>>>>                If (not(Found)) Begin
27014>>>>>>>>>                    // If the row below the deleted row was not found then it means we deleted the
27014>>>>>>>>>                    // last row. Now we will try to load the new last row. If there are no remaining
27014>>>>>>>>>                    // rows in the dataset then the buffer will be automatically cleared (which is 
27014>>>>>>>>>                    // what we want)
27014>>>>>>>>>                    If (bReverseOrdering) Begin
27016>>>>>>>>>                        Send Request_Read of hoDD FIRST_RECORD iMainFile iOrdering
27017>>>>>>>>>                    End
27017>>>>>>>>>>
27017>>>>>>>>>                    Else Begin
27018>>>>>>>>>                        Send Request_Read of hoDD LAST_RECORD iMainFile iOrdering
27019>>>>>>>>>                    End
27019>>>>>>>>>>
27019>>>>>>>>>                End
27019>>>>>>>>>>
27019>>>>>>>>>                
27019>>>>>>>>>                If (Found) Begin
27021>>>>>>>>>                    Send Request_Assign of hoDD iMainFile
27022>>>>>>>>>                End
27022>>>>>>>>>>
27022>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
27023>>>>>>>>>                    Send ClearGrid
27024>>>>>>>>>                End
27024>>>>>>>>>>
27024>>>>>>>>>                
27024>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
27025>>>>>>>>>            End
27025>>>>>>>>>>
27025>>>>>>>>>        End 
27025>>>>>>>>>>
27025>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27026>>>>>>>>>            //  Non DB-Aware handling
27026>>>>>>>>>             If (bContinue) Begin
27028>>>>>>>>>                Send RemoveRow sCurrentRowID      // Tell the client to remove the deleted row.
27029>>>>>>>>>            End
27029>>>>>>>>>>
27029>>>>>>>>>        End
27029>>>>>>>>>>
27029>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27030>>>>>>>>>    
27030>>>>>>>>>    // Client action to remove the passed row from the cache. 
27030>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RemoveRow String sRowID
27032>>>>>>>>>        String[] aParams
27033>>>>>>>>>        
27033>>>>>>>>>        Move sRowID to aParams[0]
27034>>>>>>>>>        Send ClientAction "removeRow" aParams    
27035>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27036>>>>>>>>>
27036>>>>>>>>>    // Returns true if you can move off of the selected row.
27036>>>>>>>>>    // Does nothing in cWebList. cWebList is read only. See AllowChangeSelectedRow in cWebGrid class.
27036>>>>>>>>>    Function AllowChangeSelectedRow String sGotoRow String sToRowID Returns Boolean
27038>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
27039>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27040>>>>>>>>>
27040>>>>>>>>>    // these don't do anything with lists
27040>>>>>>>>>    Procedure AppendNewRow    
27042>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27043>>>>>>>>>
27043>>>>>>>>>    // these don't do anything with lists
27043>>>>>>>>>    Procedure InsertNewRow    
27045>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27046>>>>>>>>>    
27046>>>>>>>>>    Function IndexOrder Returns Integer
27048>>>>>>>>>        // returns the sort order for subsequent DDO Request_Read calls.
27048>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering iColumnOrdering eDbGridType iConstrainFile
27048>>>>>>>>>        String iSortColumn
27048>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoColumn hoDD
27048>>>>>>>>>        
27048>>>>>>>>>        
27048>>>>>>>>>        
27048>>>>>>>>>        // if DD has an ordering we must use this
27048>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
27049>>>>>>>>>        If (hoDD > 0) Begin
27051>>>>>>>>>            Get Ordering of hoDD to iOrdering    // get the sort index from the DDO (if this has been set)
27052>>>>>>>>>            If (iOrdering<>-1) Begin
27054>>>>>>>>>                Function_Return iOrdering
27055>>>>>>>>>            End
27055>>>>>>>>>>
27055>>>>>>>>>        End
27055>>>>>>>>>>
27055>>>>>>>>>            
27055>>>>>>>>>        Get piOrdering to iOrdering
27056>>>>>>>>>        If (hoDD > 0) Begin
27058>>>>>>>>>            // this is the ordering as defined by the grid
27058>>>>>>>>>            Get Constrain_File of hoDD to iConstrainFile
27059>>>>>>>>>            // if ordering is not specified and we have a constraining parent
27059>>>>>>>>>            // we want to limit the constraint to the best choice for a constrained find
27059>>>>>>>>>            If (iOrdering=-1 and iConstrainFile) Begin
27061>>>>>>>>>                Get ConstrainedIndexOrder iConstrainFile to iOrdering
27062>>>>>>>>>            End
27062>>>>>>>>>>
27062>>>>>>>>>        End
27062>>>>>>>>>>
27062>>>>>>>>>        // if a static grid, use the grid's ordering, if dynamic we use
27062>>>>>>>>>        // the column ordering if we are sorting by a grid column, else use grid ordering
27062>>>>>>>>>        Get peDbGridType to eDbGridType
27063>>>>>>>>>        If (eDbGridType=gtAutomatic) Begin
27065>>>>>>>>>            // If we are sorting by a grid column then use that
27065>>>>>>>>>            WebGet piSortColumn to iSortColumn
27066>>>>>>>>>            
27066>>>>>>>>>            If (iSortColumn <> -1) Begin
27068>>>>>>>>>                Get GetColumnObject iSortColumn to hoColumn
27069>>>>>>>>>                If (hoColumn) Begin
27071>>>>>>>>>                    Get ColumnIndexOrder of hoColumn to iColumnOrdering      // returns -1 if there is no default index
27072>>>>>>>>>                    If (iColumnOrdering<>-1) Begin
27074>>>>>>>>>                        Move iColumnOrdering to iOrdering
27075>>>>>>>>>                    End
27075>>>>>>>>>>
27075>>>>>>>>>                End
27075>>>>>>>>>>
27075>>>>>>>>>            End
27075>>>>>>>>>>
27075>>>>>>>>>        End
27075>>>>>>>>>>
27075>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iOrdering
27076>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27077>>>>>>>>>    
27077>>>>>>>>>    
27077>>>>>>>>>    // return best index for constrained find. Return -1 which asks the runtime
27077>>>>>>>>>    // to make this choice as normally there is only one choice. 
27077>>>>>>>>>    // This is suitable for augmentation.
27077>>>>>>>>>    Function ConstrainedIndexOrder Integer iConstrainFile Returns Integer
27079>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return -1 // the runtime knows best
27080>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27081>>>>>>>>>    
27081>>>>>>>>>    
27081>>>>>>>>>    Procedure UpdateCurrentRowID
27083>>>>>>>>>        // Sets the web property psCurrentRowId for pbDataAware=True grid.
27083>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27083>>>>>>>>>        RowID riRowID
27083>>>>>>>>>        
27083>>>>>>>>>        // assert pbDataAware=True
27083>>>>>>>>>        If (not(pbDataAware(Self))) Begin
27085>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM "Assert: UpdateCurrentRowID called for non-data aware grid"
27086>>>>>>>>>>
27086>>>>>>>>>        End
27086>>>>>>>>>>
27086>>>>>>>>>        
27086>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
27087>>>>>>>>>        
27087>>>>>>>>>        If (hoDD = 0) Begin
27089>>>>>>>>>            // This will probably never happen
27089>>>>>>>>>            Move (NullRowID()) to riRowID
27090>>>>>>>>>        End
27090>>>>>>>>>>
27090>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27091>>>>>>>>>            Get CurrentRowId of hoDD to riRowID
27092>>>>>>>>>        End
27092>>>>>>>>>>
27092>>>>>>>>>        
27092>>>>>>>>>        WebSet psCurrentRowId to (SerializeRowID(riRowID))
27093>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27094>>>>>>>>>
27094>>>>>>>>>
27094>>>>>>>>>    // in sub-classes that support auto-server, which uses the
27094>>>>>>>>>    // invoking server, the server used for reading the grid may
27094>>>>>>>>>    // be different than the server defined in this view.
27094>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadingServer Returns Handle
27096>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27096>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
27097>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoDD
27098>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27099>>>>>>>>>
27099>>>>>>>>>    // This handles translation of find modes to make reverse ordering
27099>>>>>>>>>    // work. Pass the mode and return the mode, translated if reverse ordering is needed
27099>>>>>>>>>    Function FindMode Integer eFindMode Boolean bReverseOrdering Returns Integer
27101>>>>>>>>>        If (bReverseOrdering) Begin
27103>>>>>>>>>            Case Begin
27103>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=GE) ;                    Move (LE) to eFindMode
27106>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=GT) ;                    Move (LT) to eFindMode
27110>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=LT) ;                    Move (GT) to eFindMode
27114>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=LE) ;                    Move (GE) to eFindMode
27118>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=FIRST_RECORD) ;                    Move (LAST_RECORD) to eFindMode
27122>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=LAST_RECORD) ;                    Move (FIRST_RECORD) to eFindMode
27126>>>>>>>>>            Case End
27126>>>>>>>>>        End
27126>>>>>>>>>>
27126>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return eFindMode
27127>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27128>>>>>>>>>
27128>>>>>>>>>    Procedure EstablishDDFindMode Integer eFindMode Handle hoServer Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering
27130>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
27130>>>>>>>>>        Get FindMode eFindMode bReverseOrdering to eFindMode  // mode might change if reverse ordering
27131>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoServer to iFile
27132>>>>>>>>>        Send Establish_Find_Direction of hoServer eFindMode iFile iOrdering
27133>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27134>>>>>>>>>
27134>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadDDFirstRecord Handle hoDD Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering  Returns RowID
27136>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile eFindMode
27136>>>>>>>>>        // because this uses request_read it cannot be used inside of refresh
27136>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE<>0) Begin
27138>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM ("assertion failed: ReadDDFirstRecord is called when DD is busy")
27139>>>>>>>>>>
27139>>>>>>>>>        End
27139>>>>>>>>>>
27139>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoDD to iFile
27140>>>>>>>>>        Get FindMode FIRST_RECORD bReverseOrdering to eFindMode
27141>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Read of hoDD eFindMode iFile  iOrdering
27142>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (GetRowID(iFile))
27143>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27144>>>>>>>>>    
27144>>>>>>>>>    
27144>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadDDLastRecord Handle hoDD Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering  Returns RowID
27146>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile eFindMode
27146>>>>>>>>>        // because this uses request_read it cannot be used inside of refresh
27146>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE<>0) Begin
27148>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM ("assertion failed: ReadDDFirstRecord is called when DD is busy")
27149>>>>>>>>>>
27149>>>>>>>>>        End
27149>>>>>>>>>>
27149>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoDD to iFile
27150>>>>>>>>>        Get FindMode LAST_RECORD bReverseOrdering to eFindMode
27151>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Read of hoDD eFindMode iFile iOrdering
27152>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (GetRowID(iFile))
27153>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27154>>>>>>>>>    
27154>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadDDRecordInBuffer Handle hoDD Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering Returns Boolean
27156>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bFound
27156>>>>>>>>>        RowID riId
27156>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
27156>>>>>>>>>        
27156>>>>>>>>>        Send EstablishDDFindMode Ge  hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering
27157>>>>>>>>>        Send Locate_Next of hoDD
27158>>>>>>>>>        Move (Found) to bFound
27159>>>>>>>>>        If not bFound Begin
27161>>>>>>>>>            Get ReadDDLastRecord hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering to riId
27162>>>>>>>>>        End
27162>>>>>>>>>>
27162>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27163>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoDD to iFile
27164>>>>>>>>>            Move (GetRowID(iFile)) to riId
27165>>>>>>>>>        End
27165>>>>>>>>>>
27165>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (not(IsNullRowID(riId)))
27166>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27167>>>>>>>>>
27167>>>>>>>>>    // finds the record in the buffer and rebuilds the list. If the
27167>>>>>>>>>    // buffer record is not found, most likely due to a failed constraint), it
27167>>>>>>>>>    // search for the next record (where next is determined by reverse ordering).
27167>>>>>>>>>    // If there is no record, it will attemot to find the prior record. 
27167>>>>>>>>>    Procedure FindDDRecordInBuffer 
27169>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bReverseOrdering bFound
27169>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering
27169>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27169>>>>>>>>>
27169>>>>>>>>>        Get ReadingServer to hoDD
27170>>>>>>>>>        Get IndexOrder to iOrdering
27171>>>>>>>>>        WebGet pbReverseOrdering to bReverseOrdering
27172>>>>>>>>>        
27172>>>>>>>>>        Get ReadDDRecordInBuffer hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering to bFound
27173>>>>>>>>>        
27173>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
27174>>>>>>>>>        If bFound Begin
27176>>>>>>>>>            Send Request_Assign of hoDD
27177>>>>>>>>>        End
27177>>>>>>>>>>
27177>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27178>>>>>>>>>            Send ClearGrid
27179>>>>>>>>>        End
27179>>>>>>>>>>
27179>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27180>>>>>>>>>    
27180>>>>>>>>>    
27180>>>>>>>>>    // Clears the DD and creates an empty grid.
27180>>>>>>>>>    // The Clear DD behavior can work different ways with grids. Most of the time, a clear to a DD should
27180>>>>>>>>>    // just open up a new row for editing. This is consistent with what clear does everyhwere else. However, there are
27180>>>>>>>>>    // times when you need to create an empty grid. This will mostly happen when there are no valid records to display so you
27180>>>>>>>>>    // need to create an empty grid. That's what this message is for.
27180>>>>>>>>>    // For now this is public, but it needs to be used carefully. If you are clearing grids when there are records that could be
27180>>>>>>>>>    // displayed, you are fighting a normal grid behavior.
27180>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ClearGrid
27182>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bInClearGrid bDataAware
27182>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27182>>>>>>>>>        
27182>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
27183>>>>>>>>>        
27183>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware) Begin
27185>>>>>>>>>            Get pbInClearGrid to bInClearGrid
27186>>>>>>>>>            Set pbInClearGrid to True
27187>>>>>>>>>            Get Server to hoDD
27188>>>>>>>>>            Send Clear of hoDD
27189>>>>>>>>>            Set pbInClearGrid to bInClearGrid
27190>>>>>>>>>        End
27190>>>>>>>>>>
27190>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27191>>>>>>>>>            Send EmptyGridRefresh
27192>>>>>>>>>        End
27192>>>>>>>>>>
27192>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27193>>>>>>>>>    
27193>>>>>>>>>    
27193>>>>>>>>>    // Appends a row to the end of the list. It will update the user interface if needed. Should
27193>>>>>>>>>    // only be used on a manually loaded list (pbDataAware = false or peDbGridType = gtManual). 
27193>>>>>>>>>    // Implemented as a client-action meaning that it works asynchronously.
27193>>>>>>>>>    //
27193>>>>>>>>>    // Params:
27193>>>>>>>>>    //  tRow    Filled tWebRow struct with the new row data.
27193>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DataSetAppendRow tWebRow tRow
27195>>>>>>>>>        String[] aParams
27196>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow[] aRows
27196>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow[] aRows
27197>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoJson
27197>>>>>>>>>        
27197>>>>>>>>>        Move tRow to aRows[0]
27198>>>>>>>>>        
27198>>>>>>>>>        //  Convert data to JSON
27198>>>>>>>>>        Get Create (RefClass(cJsonObject)) to hoJson
27199>>>>>>>>>        Send DataTypeToJson of hoJson aRows
27200>>>>>>>>>        
27200>>>>>>>>>        Send ClientActionEx "dataSetAppendRow" aParams hoJson
27201>>>>>>>>>        Send Destroy of hoJson
27202>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27203>>>>>>>>>    
27203>>>>>>>>>    // Inserts a new row into the list before the row with the provided rowid. If the rowid is not
27203>>>>>>>>>    // found it will append the row to the end of list. Should only be used on a manually loaded
27203>>>>>>>>>    // list (pbDataAware = false or peDbGridType = gtManual). Implemented as a client-action 
27203>>>>>>>>>    // meaning that it works asynchronously.
