45332>>>>>>>>>>>// This function formats the date in a picture-string passed
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//
45332>>>>>>>>>>>// Picture  Meaning
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    d     Day of month as digits with no leading zero for single-digit days.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    dd    Day of month as digits with leading zero for single-digit days.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    ddd   Day of week as a three-letter abbreviation. The function uses the LOCALE_SABBREVDAYNAME value
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//          associated with the specified locale.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    dddd  Day of week as its full name. The function uses the LOCALE_SDAYNAME value associated with the
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//          specified locale.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    M     Month as digits with no leading zero for single-digit months.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    MM    Month as digits with leading zero for single-digit months.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    MMM   Month as a three-letter abbreviation. The function uses the LOCALE_SABBREVMONTHNAME value
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//          associated with the specified locale.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    MMMM  Month as its full name. The function uses the LOCALE_SMONTHNAME value associated with the
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//          specified locale.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    y     Year as last two digits, but with no leading zero for years less than 10.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    yy    Year as last two digits, but with leading zero for years less than 10.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    yyyy  Year represented by full four digits.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    gg    Period/era string. The function uses the CAL_SERASTRING value associated with the specified
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//          locale. This element is ignored if the date to be formatted does not have an associated era
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//          or period string.
45332>>>>>>>>>>>// For example, to get the date string
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    "Wed, Aug 31 94"
45332>>>>>>>>>>>// use the following picture string:
45332>>>>>>>>>>>//    "ddd',' MMM dd yy"
