Including file: SystemTimeAdjustment.h.pkg    (E:\Jenkins\workspace\DataFlex 26.0 - DF Source\Examples\WebOrderMobile\DfPkg\DataFlex_dev_DateTime-1.0.1\AppSrc\SystemTimeAdjustment.h.pkg)
45344>>>>>>>>>>>Use VdfBase.pkg
45344>>>>>>>>>>>
45344>>>>>>>>>>>// Determines whether the system is applying periodic time adjustments to its time-of-day clock, and obtains the value and period of any such adjustments.
45344>>>>>>>>>>>
45344>>>>>>>>>>>// Parameters
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//    lpTimeAdjustment [out]
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       a Pointer to a variable that the Function sets to the Number of lpTimeIncrement100-nanosecond units added 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       to the Time-of-day clock for every period of Time which actually passes as counted by the system. This 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       value only has meaning If lpTimeAdjustmentDisabled is False.
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//    lpTimeIncrement [out]
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       a Pointer to a variable that the Function sets to the interval in 100-nanosecond units at which the system 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       will Add lpTimeAdjustment to the Time-of-day clock. This value only has meaning If lpTimeAdjustmentDisabled is False.
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//    lpTimeAdjustmentDisabled [out]
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       a Pointer to a variable that the Function sets to indicate whether periodic Time adjustment is in effect.
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       a value of True indicates that periodic Time adjustment is disabled, and the system Time-of-day clock advances at the 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       normal rate. In this mode, the system may adjust the Time of day using its own internal Time synchronization 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       mechanisms. These internal Time synchronization mechanisms may cause the Time-of-day clock to change during the 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       normal course of the system operation, which can include noticeable jumps in Time as deemed necessary by the system.
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       a value of False indicates that periodic Time adjustment is being used to adjust the Time-of-day clock. for 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       each lpTimeIncrement period of Time that actually passes, lpTimeAdjustment will be added to the Time of day. 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       If the lpTimeAdjustment value is smaller than lpTimeIncrement, the system Time-of-day clock will advance at a rate 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       slower than normal. If the lpTimeAdjustment value is larger than lpTimeIncrement, the Time-of-day clock will advance 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       at a rate faster than normal. If lpTimeAdjustment equals lpTimeIncrement, the Time-of-day clock will advance at its 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       normal speed. The lpTimeAdjustment value can be Set by calling SetSystemTimeAdjustment. The lpTimeIncrement value is 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       fixed by the system upon start, and does not change during system operation. In this mode, the system will not interfere 
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//       with the Time adjustment scheme, and will not attempt to synchronize Time of day on its own via other techniques.
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//
45344>>>>>>>>>>>// Return Value
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//    If the Function succeeds, the return value is nonzero.
45344>>>>>>>>>>>//    If the Function fails, the return value is zero. to Get extended Error information, call GetLastError.
45344>>>>>>>>>>>
45344>>>>>>>>>>>External_Function WINAPI_GetSystemTimeAdjustment "GetSystemTimeAdjustment" Kernel32.dll ;    Pointer lpTimeAdjustment ;    Pointer lpTimeIncrement ;    Pointer lpTimeAdjustmentDisabled ;    Returns Boolean
