55591>>>>>>>    // The AddFilter function expects a string. If you move a DateTime to a string the format
55591>>>>>>>    // is incorrect for SQL. With this function we can convert the DateTime to string in the appropriate
55591>>>>>>>    // format (this is yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss)). The prefix zeroes are important.
55591>>>>>>>    Function DateTimeToString DateTime dtIn Returns String
55593>>>>>>>        String sDateTimeResult
55593>>>>>>>
55593>>>>>>>        Move (DateGetYear (dtIn)) to sDateTimeResult
55594>>>>>>>        Move (sDateTimeResult - '-' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetMonth (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateTimeResult
55595>>>>>>>        Move (sDateTimeResult - '-' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetDay (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateTimeResult
55596>>>>>>>        Move (sDateTimeResult * (Right ('0' + String (DateGetHour (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateTimeResult
55597>>>>>>>        Move (sDateTimeResult - ':' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetMinute (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateTimeResult
55598>>>>>>>        Move (sDateTimeResult - ':' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetSecond (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateTimeResult
55599>>>>>>>
55599>>>>>>>        Function_Return sDateTimeResult
55600>>>>>>>    End_Function
55601>>>>>>>
55601>>>>>>>    // The AddFilter function expects a string. If you move a Date to a string the format
55601>>>>>>>    // is incorrect for SQL. With this function we can convert the Date to string first in the appropriate
55601>>>>>>>    // format (this is yyyy-mm-dd). The prefix zero's are important.
55601>>>>>>>    Function DateToString Date dIn Returns String
55603>>>>>>>        String sDateResult
55603>>>>>>>        DateTime dtIn
55603>>>>>>>
55603>>>>>>>        Move dIn to dtIn
55604>>>>>>>        Move (DateGetYear (dtIn)) to sDateResult
55605>>>>>>>        Move (sDateResult - '-' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetMonth (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateResult
55606>>>>>>>        Move (sDateResult - '-' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetDay (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateResult
55607>>>>>>>
55607>>>>>>>        Function_Return sDateResult
55608>>>>>>>    End_Function
55609>>>>>>>
55609>>>>>>>    // Use this function to convert a time variable to string. Should be used for psParameterValue.
55609>>>>>>>    Function TimeToString Time tmIn Returns String
55611>>>>>>>        String sTimeResult
55611>>>>>>>        DateTime dtIn
55611>>>>>>>
55611>>>>>>>        Move tmIn to dtIn
55612>>>>>>>        Move (Right ('0' + String (DateGetHour (dtIN)), 2)) to sTimeResult
55613>>>>>>>        Move (sTimeResult + ':' + Right ('0' + String (DateGetMinute (dtIn)), 2)) to sTimeResult
55614>>>>>>>        Move (sTimeResult + ':' + Right ('0' + String (DateGetSecond (dtIn)), 2)) to sTimeResult
55615>>>>>>>
55615>>>>>>>        Function_Return sTimeResult
55616>>>>>>>    End_Function
55617>>>>>>>End_Class
