62172>>>// This example webview is the second part of the orderlist report example. The component contains the report object, which
62172>>>// will be invoked from the cWebDRReportViewer class to produce a HTML "stream". The returned String array contains all
62172>>>// pages of the report. The javascript counterpart (previewer.js) shows the result and the user can navigate thru the pages.
62172>>>// The cWebDRReportViewer control allows printing of the report thru the browser and via the action menu the user can select
62172>>>// to export the report to one of the supported formats.
62172>>>// Note that for this the report and the data will be reloaded, reformatted. Theoretically the results can be different
62172>>>// due to changed data in the database.
62172>>>
62172>>>// The minimum order total value entered in the selections webview is passed via a NamedValue in the NavigateData parameter.
62172>>>
62172>>>// The language passed from the browser (the client language) is used to overrule the settings from the server for date and
62172>>>// number formatting and for a currency symbol. In a real world a currency symbol change should also mean a recalculation of
62172>>>// the amount. For this example we just do as if the value is correct for the currency symbol.
62172>>>
62172>>>Object oOrderListReportResults is a cWebView
62174>>>    Set psCaption to "Order List (Results)"
62175>>>    Set pbShowCaption to False
62176>>>    Set peViewType to vtZoom
