62671>>>// This example webview is the second part of the Sales per Salesperson per USA state crosstab report. The component
62671>>>// contains the report Object, which will be invoked from the cWebDRReportViewer class to produce a HTML "stream".
62671>>>// The returned String array contains all pages of the report. The javascript counterpart (previewer.js) shows the
62671>>>// result and the user can navigate thru the pages. The cWebDRReportViewer control allows printing of the report
62671>>>// thru the browser and via the action menu the user can select to export the report to one of the supported formats.
62671>>>// Note that for this the report and the data will be reloaded, reformatted. Theoretically the results can be different
62671>>>// due to changed data in the database.
62671>>>
62671>>>// The language passed from the browser (the client language) is used to overrule the settings from the server for date and
62671>>>// number formatting and for a currency symbol. In a real world a currency symbol change should also mean a recalculation of
62671>>>// the amount. For this example it is used for the date format in the page footer.
62671>>>
62671>>>Object oSalesPerSalesPersonPerUSAStateReportResults is a cWebView
62673>>>    Set psCaption to "Sales per Salesperson per USA State (Results)"
62674>>>    Set pbShowCaption to False
62675>>>    Set peViewType to vtZoom
62676>>>    Set peWebViewStyle to wvsDrillDown
62677>>>    Set peStateMode to vsmOff
62678>>>    Set psStateViewName to "SalesPerSalesPersonPerUSAStateReportResults"
62679>>>
62679>>>    Object oReport is a cDRReport
62681>>>        Set psReportName to "Sales per Salesperson per USA state.dr"
62682>>>
62682>>>        Procedure OnInitializeReport
62685>>>            String sReportId
62685>>>            String[] sBrowserLanguages
62686>>>
62686>>>            Get psReportId to sReportId
62687>>>
62687>>>            Send SetFilters sReportId
62688>>>            Send SetParameters sReportId
62689>>>
62689>>>            // Get the preferred browser (client) language and pass this on to the report
62689>>>            WebGet pasBrowserLanguages of ghoWebApp to sBrowserLanguages
62690>>>            If (SizeOfArray (sBrowserLanguages) > 0) Begin
62692>>>                Send SetReportLocaleAndLanguage sReportId sBrowserLanguages[0] 'ReportLanguage'
62693>>>            End
62693>>>>
62693>>>        End_Procedure
62694>>>
62694>>>        Procedure SetFilters String sReportId
62697>>>            tWebNavigateData NavigateData
62697>>>            tWebNavigateData NavigateData
62697>>>            Integer iCustomerStatus iCustomerStatusMode
62697>>>
62697>>>            Get GetNavigateData to NavigateData
62698>>>            Get NamedValueIndex NavigateData.NamedValues "CustomerStatus" to iCustomerStatus
62699>>>            Get NamedValueIndex NavigateData.NamedValues "CustomerStatusMode" to iCustomerStatusMode
62700>>>
62700>>>            If (iCustomerStatusMode > -1 and iCustomerStatus > -1) Begin
62702>>>                Send AddFilter sReportId "{Customer.Status}" NavigateData.NamedValues[iCustomerStatusMode].sValue NavigateData.NamedValues[iCustomerStatus].sValue
62703>>>            End
62703>>>>
62703>>>        End_Procedure
62704>>>
62704>>>        // In this routine we find the code that sets the parameter values. The values
62704>>>        // for the parameters can be retrieved from an input control or from own coding.
62704>>>        Procedure SetParameters String sReportId
62707>>>            Integer iParameter
62707>>>            String sTotalsPerState
62707>>>            String sTotalsPerSalesPerson
62707>>>            String sGrandTotal
