64567>
64567>    // Generates a string of 40 random characters between ASCII 33 & ASCII 126
64567>    // This should produce a unique string suitable for a 16 character encryption key.
64567>    // Excludes the ;"' characters.
64567>    //
64567>    // Used by WebApps to give the psEncryptPassword property a unique value.
64567>    Function GenerateEncryptString Returns String
64570>        Integer i iASCII
64570>        String sChar sKey
64570>
64570>        For i from 0 to 39
64576>            Move (Random(93)) to iASCII
64577>            Move (iASCII + 34) to iASCII
64578>
64578>            If (iASCII = 34 or iASCII = 39 or iASCII = 59) Begin
64580>                Increment iASCII
64581>            End
64581>
64581>            Move (Character(iASCII)) to sChar
64582>            Move (sKey + sChar) to sKey
64583>        Loop
64584>
64584>        Function_Return sKey
64585>    End_Function
64586>
64586>
64586>    Procedure InitPassword
64589>        // Note to the developer: For security purposes each installation of the this workspace must
64589>        // contain a unique value for the framework's encryption key. This value is stored in the cWebApp
64589>        // object's psEncryptPassword property.
64589>        //
64589>        // To ensure each running installation of WebOrder is different we have modified the Web App
64589>        // to generate a random psEncryptPassword value the first time that it is run. This value is
64589>        // then used and is stored in the OrdSys system table so that it does not get re-generated
64589>        // in subsequent instances of this web application.
64589>        //
64589>        // Since this workspace is installed and run automatically when you install DataFlex we are required
64589>        // to ensure that the encryption password cannot be guessed. Normally you would not need, or want, to
64589>        // use this technique in your own web applications. Instead you would manually set psEncryptPassword
64589>        // to a trusted, unique value for each web application that you deploy.
64589>
64589>
64589>        // Test if an encryption password has already been generated.
64589>        If (Trim(OrderSystem.EncryptPassword) = "") Begin
64591>            Reread OrderSystem
64595>            // Just in case another instance wrote to OrdSys.EncryptPassword in the millisecond
64595>            // between the above two lines of code we will test this value again
64595>            If (Trim(OrderSystem.EncryptPassword) = "") Begin
64597>                Get GenerateEncryptString to OrderSystem.EncryptPassword
64598>                SaveRecord OrderSystem
64599>            End
64599>            Unlock
64600>        End
64600>
64600>        Set psEncryptPassword to (Trim(OrderSystem.EncryptPassword))
64601>    End_Procedure
64602>
64602>    Send InitPassword
64603>End_Object
64604>
64604>Send StartWebApp of oWebApp
